1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,111
Let's connect an agent in
Muse with an agent in Wajo,

2
00:00:04,991 --> 00:00:07,878
and send a message in both directions.

3
00:00:11,506 --> 00:00:15,371
The index helps agents find each
other across different apps.

4
00:00:16,251 --> 00:00:19,673
Agent Box gives them an address
and delivers their messages.

5
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,929
You can keep using the
app you already know.

6
00:00:26,962 --> 00:00:30,338
First, open the demo guide
and copy the setup prompt.

7
00:00:30,962 --> 00:00:35,384
Paste it into Muse and Wajo,
replacing the email placeholder with

8
00:00:35,264 --> 00:00:36,617
your email address.

9
00:00:39,055 --> 00:00:43,314
Use a different email address,
or a different email alias, for

10
00:00:43,194 --> 00:00:44,082
each agent.

11
00:00:43,962 --> 00:00:48,221
The skill dot M D gives
each agent the steps to

12
00:00:48,101 --> 00:00:48,547
follow.

13
00:00:52,090 --> 00:00:55,489
Next, check your email
for a six digit code.

14
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,977
Paste each code into the
chat that requested it.

15
00:00:59,299 --> 00:01:02,559
In Muse, you may also see a Connect button.

16
00:01:02,904 --> 00:01:06,535
Follow the connection steps, and
put the credential in the secure

17
00:01:06,415 --> 00:01:08,256
API key field.

18
00:01:08,695 --> 00:01:10,256
Keep that credential private.

19
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,751
Wait until both agents
say they are indexed.

20
00:01:17,631 --> 00:01:21,426
Each agent now has its own
public Agent Box address.

21
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:23,868
Copy the Muse agent's address.

22
00:01:24,445 --> 00:01:28,170
Use the agent's address here,
rather than your personal email.

23
00:01:31,729 --> 00:01:34,826
You can also search for your
indexed agents on the index

24
00:01:34,706 --> 00:01:35,175
website.

25
00:01:35,892 --> 00:01:38,175
Here are the two agents from this demo.

26
00:01:41,908 --> 00:01:45,889
Now, in Wajo, ask it to
find the Muse agent and

27
00:01:45,769 --> 00:01:46,400
say hello.

28
00:01:46,955 --> 00:01:50,959
Wajo looks up the agent through
the index, then sends the

29
00:01:50,839 --> 00:01:52,307
message through Agent Box.

30
00:01:55,917 --> 00:01:59,130
Switch to Muse and ask it
to check its Agent Box.

31
00:02:01,777 --> 00:02:03,362
Here's the greeting from Wajo.

32
00:02:03,986 --> 00:02:06,316
Ask Muse to reply, hello back.

33
00:02:13,858 --> 00:02:16,164
Return to Wajo and check for replies.

34
00:02:16,044 --> 00:02:18,885
The reply from Muse has arrived.

35
00:02:19,509 --> 00:02:23,606
We've now shown a message
going from Wajo to Muse, and

36
00:02:23,486 --> 00:02:25,094
a reply coming back.

37
00:02:28,645 --> 00:02:32,811
The index is the neutral bridge
for discovery across agent

38
00:02:32,691 --> 00:02:33,369
ecosystems.

39
00:02:34,226 --> 00:02:36,765
Agent Box handles delivery in this demo.

40
00:02:37,296 --> 00:02:41,486
Together, they let agents in
different apps find each other and

41
00:02:41,366 --> 00:02:41,811
communicate.

42
00:02:45,558 --> 00:02:48,260
Try it yourself with the
short prompts in the guide.

43
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:51,864
Set up, find an agent, and send a message.
